SUMMARY:CoffeeTue- HS Rise Bake Shop (31F) C/D Pace-- RSVP required
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nRide Leader: (volunteer t
 o lead!)\nRide Sweep: Rick Zook\n\nCoffeeTue rides:\n• A rotating start 
 location\, not a school\n• A predetermined route\n• 25+/- mile routes\
 n• 12 to 14 and 14 to 17 mph average pace\n• “short” stop for refr
 eshment/coffee mid-route at [Rise Bake Shoppe](https://www.risebakeshoppe.
 com/)\n\nLike an All Class Ride\, CoffeeTue does not have a single pace.\n
 As Sweep\, Rick Zook will bike with any "D" ride cyclist.\nThe CoffeeTue r
 ides are social rides\, but cyclists are not expected to stay in one group
 . Cyclists may pedal at their own comfortable paces. A planned stop to reg
 roup is recommended. Please be supportive of the other cyclists to avoid a
 nyone biking alone or being dropped off the back of the last group.\n**Be 
 Safe\, Have Fun\, and Ride Together**\n\nClick for [Ride with GPS](https:/
 /routes.lancasterbikeclub.net/cue/hs-rise-bake-shop-31f/)\n\nHelmets are m
 andatory. No ear buds. Please bring water and a basic repair kit (spare tu
 be\, tire levers\, pump/CO2 inflator).\n\nTo eliminate passing around a pe
 n and paper waiver\, we require LBC Club membership and Meetup RSVP below 
 to join this ride.\n\nBeing on Meetup does not mean you are a club member.
  [Join here](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&clu
 b_id=257148).\n\nYour RSVP is your agreement to abide by the club's [Code 
 of Conduct](https://lancbikeclub.clubexpress.com/content.aspx?page_id=22&c
 lub_id=257148&module_id=323984) \,\n[Rules of the Road](https://lancbikecl
 ub.clubexpress.com/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=325159
 ) \, and [Ride Waiver](https://lancasterbikeclub.net/docs.ashx?id=454318)\
 nIn case of accident\, consult the [Ride Leader Guide](https://s3.amazonaw
 s.com/ClubExpressClubFiles/257148/documents/Ride_Leader_Guide_2026_1233574
 28.pdf?AWSAccessKeyId=AKIA6MYUE6DNNJ6ROIH3&Expires=1778249903&response-con
 tent-disposition=inline%3B%20filename%3DRide_Leader_Guide_2026.pdf&Signatu
 re=pwxGJ6nqlu4w9Zj8Kj%2Fl9U5%2BBtQ%3D).
